class RunSection(_RunSectionRequired, _RunSectionOptional):
    """run: The run this section is about: one that records names.
    tool: The run's receipt head's tool (spec §5), as the loader read it.
    v: The run's receipt head's v (spec §5), as the loader read it.
    argv: The run's receipt head's argv (spec §5), already redacted there (spec §5.3). Never cut part-way: when it does not fit the section's bound it is dropped whole and named in dropped.
    resolved: The run's receipt head's resolved (spec §5): its interpretation after defaults, environment and path resolution, copied whole and already redacted there (spec §5.3), so a reader can tell, say, which commits a run compared without opening the head (flyingrobots/parley#90). Its shape is the tool's; the reader chooses none of its keys. Never cut part-way: when it does not fit the section's bound it is dropped whole, first of all fields, and named in dropped. Absent when the window does not hold the head or the head's resolved is not an object.
    inv: The run's inv (spec §2.2): the head's, or else the window's receipt.inputs for the run. Absent when neither carries one; never a placeholder.
    outcome: What the records in the window establish about the run: failed for an error, a startup failure or a non-zero end; succeeded for an end of 0 and nothing against it; undetermined otherwise (spec §1.2a). It is the window's verdict, not the digest's: a run whose end the bound cut is still succeeded. Absent when the reader established none.
    reason: Why the outcome is undetermined, present exactly when it is. no_end_in_window: the window holds no end for the run, which cannot say whether the run ended later or never did. end_status_unusable: the window holds an end whose status is not a number.
    head: Present when the window does not hold the run's receipt head, so tool, v and argv are not known from it. Absent when it does.
    folded: Present when this run stands for other runs of the same invocation and the same result (flyingrobots/parley#79): runs with an equal inv (spec §2.2) whose outcome, reason, end status, error, warning and startup-failure codes and head's resolved are equal too, and whose result records are equal one for one in seq order: the tool's own records and any other record the protocol does not define, each page, each sidecar by its bytes and sha256, and a read's own lens without its session and the query it names, compared without the envelope's t, seq and run (flyingrobots/parley#133). A top-level session on a record of the tool's own or on a page is that record's own field and is compared (flyingrobots/parley#146). Under a view whose surface holds decision records those are equal as well, compared the same way: receipt.step under how-it-decided and everything, cache.hit under those two and what-ran. A decision record of a kind the view's surface does not hold is not compared, so runs that differ only in such records still stand for one another. Every comparison here is of the records the window holds: two runs whose results in the window differ are a divergence (spec §2.3) and do not stand for one another, and a run only partly inside the window is compared by the part the window holds, so runs that stand for one another under one window can differ under a wider one. A section marks a run the window did not hold whole in two cases: head not_in_window when the window does not hold the run's head, and outcome undetermined with reason no_end_in_window when it holds no end for the run and no failure either; a run the window shows to have failed is failed with or without its end, so its section does not say whether the window holds the end. This run is the most recent of them, by the latest t among each run's records in the window and, where those are equal, the greater run id; the others' records are not named, and stands_for lists the others' run ids. A run with no inv in the window, a run the window shows to be redacted (its head carries redacted, an end in the window states redacted true, or the window holds a redaction event of the run), and a run the window does not show to be unredacted, because it holds neither the run's receipt head nor an end that states redacted false, do not stand for another (spec §1.2a, §2.3). A run that stands for no other has no folded. Never dropped to fit the section's bound.
    dropped: The fields left out, whole, to bound the section's serialised JSON, in the order they were dropped, each at most once: resolved, then argv, then inv, then v, then tool. The bound is the reader's to state (parley-read: 512 UTF-8 bytes); a string or an object is never cut part-way.
    """
