class Lens(_LensRequired, _LensOptional):
    """The lens a result carries: the asker, the view, the budget and the window that produced it, the query it answers, a stated bound on what the view loses, and the records it was built from by (run, seq) (spec §9, informative; decided in flyingrobots/parley#46). One lens line precedes the result it describes, so a later reader knows what it is looking at and can get back to the records.

    Message `parley.lens`, schema version `1.1.0`.

    t: POSIX time in milliseconds (spec §1.3).
    seq: The run's single counter (spec §1.3).
    run: The execution this line belongs to: the read itself, not the runs being read (spec §2.1).
    session: Working period spanning runs. Supplied by the caller or inherited; never invented (spec §2.1).
    query: The recorded query this result answers, by (run, seq). Required: §9 records every query, and a result whose query was not recorded cannot be audited.
    asker: Echoed from the query: who the result is for.
    view: The view this result is. Echoed from the query, from the same closed set.
    budget: The budget actually applied, including a default the query did not supply. Constitutive, not decoration: two results computed under different budgets are not comparable, so a lens without it does not identify the view that produced the result.
    window: The stretch of history the result covers, echoed from the query.
    fold: Echoed from the query, present exactly when the query states it (flyingrobots/parley#133). false: the read folded nothing, so loss.folded is 0 and no runs section carries folded because none was allowed to, not because no runs repeated. Two results over one window, one folded and one not, are not comparable, so a lens says which it is.
    loss: What the view loses against the records it was built from, so a later reader knows which questions this result can still answer and cannot mistake a digest for the whole. A digest that folded runs names fewer records than it stands for, and says how many in folded.
    runs: One section per run that records names, in the order records first names it, and none for any other run (flyingrobots/parley#83). It states once what is true of every record of the run — which invocation it was and what became of it — rather than on each entry. Read off the window's records when the lens is built, so it cannot drift from the head it summarises. Part of the line budget.bytes bounds. Optional so that lines written under the earlier drafts still validate; parley-read always writes it.
    records: The records this result was built from, by (run, seq), never more than budget.records of them. Stored rather than recomputed: projecting down to a result is cheap and expanding back up may be impossible within a budget, so the way back has to be written here. A result is built from records, never from another result. Each entry may also carry a fixed summary of the record it names — event, t and, on an error or warning, its code — so a reader can choose what to open without opening it (flyingrobots/parley#77, flyingrobots/parley#83). What is true of the entry's whole run, its identity and outcome, is stated once in runs. The summary is read off the record when the lens is built and is part of the line budget.bytes bounds.
    """
